blocking_findings: F1 The daemon guard never selects a real serve --service daemon. daemon_pids (review-run.sh:419-425, judge-run.sh:314-320) reads /proc/<pid>/cmdline as utf8 and tests argv.includes("serve --service") on the raw buffer, but Linux separates real argv elements with NUL bytes: a daemon started as 'opencode.exe serve --service' (the incident shape recorded at measure/runs/opencode_host_isolation/record-3.1.log:21 and measure/tracks/opencode_host_isolation/spec.md:28) has cmdline '...opencode.exe\0serve\0--service', which does not contain the space-joined substring. Verified with a node check: the NUL-separated shape does not match; a single argument that embeds the text does. The only matching shape is the test fake's crafted argv[0] ('fake-opencode serve --service <tag>' via exec -a, fake-opencode spawn_daemon_child). Consequence: on every wired path the guard finds no real daemon, sends no TERM or KILL, prints no INFRA line, and the records hold no infra field, while D1/D3/D2/JD1 pass. Fix: normalize the cmdline before matching (argv.replace(/\0/g, " ").includes("serve --service"), or split on NUL and require the token pair), and give the fake daemon a real token split so the tests pin the real shape.
nonblocking_findings: N1 The review-run gate is timing-flaky under load: the first rerun printed '61 pass / 1 fail' (R12 caught a live model-call wrapper of an earlier case), the immediate second run printed '62 pass / 0 fail'; a concurrent judge-run test run of another session was active near 04:35. N2 The HOME guards are tautological as written: provider-credential.sh:97 calls check_job_home with the constant "$FOLDER/home", and review-run.sh:662-665 / judge-run.sh:446-449 compare "$JOB/home" against "$JOB"/*, true for every JOB except "/"; the effective protection is the fixed HOME env of run_opencode/run_model_call plus the S5/JS2 one-real-HOME-call assertions. N3 daemon_pid_alive hardcodes /proc/<pid>/stat while daemon_pids honors BENCH_OPENCODE_PROC (review-run.sh:440-448 vs 433; judge-run.sh:294-302 vs 328); no production impact, but the two helpers disagree. N4 run_seed_export (provider-credential.sh:159) takes its cwd folder from "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}"; an operator TMPDIR inside a git work tree breaks the 4.13o rule 'cwd in an empty folder outside any git repo'.
